            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The following works:\n\n```\nclass Test2(Test):\n    exec(\"\"\"\ndef _test(self) -> int:\n        return 1\"\"\", locals(), locals())\n\nt = Test2(name=\"test\")\nprint(t._test())\n```\n\nThat suggests to me (although I haven't done a thorough search) that Pydantic has a type test to see if an attribute is an exact Python function (i.e. `types.FunctionType`). Unfortunately we can't possibly meet such a check. If that is the case then it's only solvable by Pydantic.",
