        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "One more comment. This fails in the same way as Cython when run in Python (with no Cython involved):\n\n```\nclass Callable:\n    def __call__(_self, self):\n        return 1\n\nclass Test2(Test):\n    _test = Callable()\n\nt = Test2(name=\"test\")\nprint(t._test())\n```\n\nThat's very strong evidence that it's an exact type check and not really a Cython failure. I'll close this for now, but if you come up with anything to contradict my view then do comment and we can have another look.",
